e.\", \"confidence\": 0.35}], \"summary\": \"The FCC's address strapping for the PCA9685 PWM driver (A0 tied high, giving 0x41 rather than the specified 0x40) and the FCC HSE crystal routed to PE6/PE7 instead of the H7 oscillator pins PH0/PH1 both deviate from the intended design. The first is the more clearly supported finding.\"}",
